WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
Particle physics keeps strict accounts.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:07.640
Some quantities are the same before
and after every interaction and decay.

3
00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.020
Charge is always one of them.

4
00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:13.370
Now imagine a single proton
changing into a positron,

5
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.410
plus a flash of light.

6
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.430
Charge balances: plus
1 before, plus 1 after.

7
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.050
Energy balances too.

8
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.930
So the books look clean.

9
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.430
What forbids it?

10
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.970
In this mission, you'll audit
reactions the careful way:

11
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.410
add up the left side,
add up the right side,

12
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.390
one quantity at a time.

13
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.100
Then you'll judge proposed
decays, allowed or forbidden,

14
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.660
knowing that one broken law
is enough to rule one out.

15
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:45.010
Your mission: find out what forbids the
proton's decay to a positron plus light.
